    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes. BUILD SUCCESS.\n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property (readOnly integer, 0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n\n2. **`LuhnCheckDigit.java`** (new util) \u2014 A small single-responsibility class computing the Luhn check digit over the digits in a string (rightmost-digit doubled, non-digits skipped), matching the standard algorithm. Returns `null` for `null` input, consistent with the other formatters.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` wiring `checkDigit` to `LuhnCheckDigit.compute(owner.getCustomerCode())`, alongside the existing derived-field mappings.\n\nThis mirrors the existing pattern (each derived value lives in its own util invoked from the mapper) rather than piling logic into an existing class. Full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
